# {{Project}} GUI

The web frontend of {{project}}, made with `yuno-skeleton project` (its
`gui/`).

Built with [Vite](https://vitejs.dev/) and the Yunetas
`@yuneta/gobj-js` framework on top of the declarative shell
(`C_YUI_SHELL` + `C_YUI_NAV`) of `@yuneta/gobj-ui`. Both come from the
npm registry: a change to the library reaches this app once it is
published and the range in `package.json` is raised.

The app runs with `set_strings_are_text(true)`: a plain string given to
`createElement2()` is text, and markup is said with `html_markup()`. The
`prebuild` runs the check gobj-ui publishes
(`check-markup-strings.mjs`); it cannot see markup a helper RETURNS, so
before deploying, load the app and read the console for the
`html_markup()` warnings.

{{description}}

## Status

Skeleton.  Every menu route resolves to the placeholder gclass
`C_{{PROJECT}}_VIEW`.  Replace it with real views as you build them.

## Bootstrap

```bash
npm install
npm run dev    # http://localhost:5173
npm run build  # validate-locales + check-markup, then vite build
```

## Layout

```
gui/
├── config.json          — title, metadata, CSP origins (consumed by Vite plugin)
├── index.html
├── vite.config.js       — dedupe of the libraries gobj-ui shares with the app
├── package.json
├── public/              — static assets served at the site root
│   ├── 404.html
│   ├── browserconfig.xml
│   ├── humans.txt
│   ├── robots.txt
│   └── site.webmanifest
└── src/
    ├── app_config.json  — declarative shell + menu tree
    ├── c_{{project}}_app.js  — the app's service: handles the toolbar's events (language)
    ├── c_{{project}}_view.js — placeholder view gclass (title/subtitle are i18n keys)
    ├── main.js          — registers gclasses, sets up i18n, starts the yuno
    └── locales/
        ├── en.js        — English translations
        ├── es.js        — Spanish translations
        ├── flags.js     — SVG flags for the language switcher
        └── locales.js   — i18next bootstrap
```

## Gotchas

- **Inline `<script>` is blocked by CSP.**  `yunetaHtmlPlugin` emits
  `script-src 'self'`, so anything that needs to run before the
  bundle (anti-FOUC, theme bootstrap, feature detection) must live
  in `public/<name>.js` and be referenced with
  `<script src="/<name>.js">`.  `eval()` and `new Function()` are
  also forbidden by the policy.

- **Log in through a BFF from the dev server: the `Origin` is the dev
  server's.**  When `vite.config.js` proxies `/auth` to an `auth_bff`
  (`server.proxy`, with `changeOrigin: true`), the proxy rewrites only
  the `Host`. The BFF serves a login, refresh or logout only to the
  `Origin` of its SPA (its `allowed_origin`), so a BFF with the
  production `allowed_origin` answers every request of the dev server
  `403 origin_not_allowed`, and its `error` names both origins. A logout
  refused this way leaves the `HttpOnly` cookies, and a reload restores
  the session. Either give the dev BFF the origin of the dev server
  (`"allowed_origin": "http://localhost:5173"`), or make the proxy send
  the allowed one:

  ```javascript
  proxy: {
      "/auth": {
          target: "https://localhost:<bff port>",
          changeOrigin: true,
          secure: false,
          headers: {origin: "https://<the allowed_origin of the BFF>"}
      }
  }
  ```

- **Don't restyle gobj-ui internals.**  The shell owns its own DOM
  and CSS (toolbar, drawers, dropdowns, navs).  Before adding a
  selector that targets a framework hook in app CSS, see whether
  the need can be expressed by extending `app_config.json` (a new
  `type` / `action.type` / `show_on` value) or by a public helper of
  the library. See gobj-ui's `SHELL.md` §0 for the declarative-first
  order of preference.

## Add a real view

1. Implement the view as a Yuneta GClass exposing a `$container`
   `HTMLElement` attribute (see `c_{{project}}_view.js` for the
   contract).
2. Register it in `main.js`.
3. Replace the relevant `target.gclass` in `app_config.json` and pass
   any initial attributes via `target.kw`.  Setting
   `target.kw.subtitle` also seeds the hover tooltip for free.

